\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Comprehensive Cosmological Dynamics and Observables on $K3 \times T^2$.} (a) Modulus flow $\tau (t) = x(t) + i y(t)$ on the upper half-plane $\mathbb  {H}$ relaxing from high-energy initial conditions toward the fixed points $\tau = i/\sqrt  {12}$ and $\tau = e^{i\pi /3}$ (Kummer orbifold point); a previously reported minimum $\qopname  \relax m{min}(y) = 0.289$ is inconsistent with the fundamental-domain bound $y \ge \sqrt  {3}/2$ derived in the text and could not be traced to any output field in this repository, so it is withdrawn pending an identified source. (b) Dark energy equation of state $w_\phi (t) = (T-V)/(T+V)$, bounded from below by $w(t) \ge -1$ when $V \ge 0$ (ruling out phantom energy in that regime; see text for scope). (c) Symmetron non-linear screening scalar profile $\phi (r)/\phi _0$ across the stellar/halo core ($r \le 1$), revealing interior suppression $\phi (0)/\phi _0 = 1.97\times 10^{-14}$ and thin-shell screening $\Delta R/R \approx 1.18\times 10^{-4}$ (simulation output; not yet reconciled with the analytic thin-shell estimate, see text). (d) Cosmic energy density transitions showing radiation, matter, and modulus dark energy domination ($\Omega _r \to \Omega _m \to \Omega _\phi $).\relax }}{29}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cosmo_simulations}{{2}{29}{\textbf {Comprehensive Cosmological Dynamics and Observables on $K3 \times T^2$.} (a) Modulus flow $\tau (t) = x(t) + i y(t)$ on the upper half-plane $\mathbb {H}$ relaxing from high-energy initial conditions toward the fixed points $\tau = i/\sqrt {12}$ and $\tau = e^{i\pi /3}$ (Kummer orbifold point); a previously reported minimum $\min (y) = 0.289$ is inconsistent with the fundamental-domain bound $y \ge \sqrt {3}/2$ derived in the text and could not be traced to any output field in this repository, so it is withdrawn pending an identified source. (b) Dark energy equation of state $w_\phi (t) = (T-V)/(T+V)$, bounded from below by $w(t) \ge -1$ when $V \ge 0$ (ruling out phantom energy in that regime; see text for scope). (c) Symmetron non-linear screening scalar profile $\phi (r)/\phi _0$ across the stellar/halo core ($r \le 1$), revealing interior suppression $\phi (0)/\phi _0 = \numreconcile {1.97\times 10^{-14}}{\texttt {interior\_suppression}}$ and thin-shell screening $\Delta R/R \approx \numreconcile {1.18\times 10^{-4}}{\texttt {screening\_factor}}$ (simulation output; not yet reconciled with the analytic thin-shell estimate, see text). (d) Cosmic energy density transitions showing radiation, matter, and modulus dark energy domination ($\Omega _r \to \Omega _m \to \Omega _\phi $).\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
