\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Serverless Spot GPU/TPU Scaling and Cost Economics for Cosmological Parameter Sweeps.} (a) Cumulative compute cost for a large-scale cosmological parameter sweep (illustrative scale; not a specific run recorded in this repository) comparing dedicated 128-core HPC clusters (\$18.50/hr), on-demand cloud GPU (\$0.70/hr), serverless spot TPU v5e (\$0.36/hr), and serverless spot Nvidia L4 (\$0.20/hr, min=0); these per-hour rates are indicative and not sourced to a dated rate card in this repository. When the sweep terminates at 300s, serverless resources scale to zero instantly. (b) Throughput scaling (time-steps/second) across spatial grid resolutions ($32^2$ to $512^2$); throughput relative to any baseline solver is pending hardware verification, as no benchmark harness, execution log, or named baseline solver for this comparison exists in this repository.\relax }}{37}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
